sages are deleted (purged or received by an application) and", "direction": "in", "documented_values": [{"description": "Brings up the MSMQ console (debug version).", "token": "MACHINE_ACTION_CONSOLE"}, {"description": "Connects the computer to the network and to the directory service.", "token": "MACHINE_ACTION_CONNECT"}, {"description": "Disconnects the computer from the network and from the directory service.", "token": "MACHINE_ACTION_DISCONNECT"}, {"description": "Exits manual mode.", "token": "MACHINE_ACTION_EXIT"}, {"description": "Stops the MSMQ service.", "token": "MACHINE_ACTION_SHUTDOWN"}, {"description": "Starts the MSMQ service.", "token": "MACHINE_ACTION_STARTUP"}, {"description": "Cleans up empty message files every six hours. This is helpful when many messages are deleted (purged or received by an application) and the application needs the disk space available immediately.", "token": "MACHINE_ACTION_TIDY"}, {"description": "Deletes a message in the queue.", "token": "QUEUE_ACTION_DELMSG"}, {"description": "Resends the pending transaction sequence.", "token": "QUEUE_ACTION_EOD_RESEND"}, {"description": "Valid for outgoing queues only. Stops the sending of messages from the computer. The queue manager will not send messages to the applicable destination queue until a RESUME action is initiated.", "token": "QUEUE_ACTION_PAUSE"}, {"description": "Purges the queue (deletes all messages in the queue). Use MQMgmtAction with this option. MSMQ does not support a separate MQPurgeQueue function like the desktop version of MSMQ.", "token": "QUEUE_ACTION_PURGE"}, {"description": "Only valid for outgoing queues. Restarts the sending of messages after a PAUSE action has been initiated.", "token": "QUEUE_ACTION_RESUME"}], "evidence_status": "documented", "name": "pAction", "position": null, "type": null, "type_raw": null}], "parse": {"model": "c_declarator_v1", "notes": ["unnamed_parameter:1", "unnamed_parameter:2", "unnamed_parameter:3"], "status": "parsed"}, "retu